@@ -9,10 +9,24 @@ Implemented a scroll-scrubbed hero with approximately 15 stable viewport heights
 The directory guard now enumerates both campaign photo directories, covering all 480 and 960 derivatives. A temporary unlisted photo caused `npx tsx --test tests/arrival-campaign-media.test.ts` to fail with the expected unprotected-photo assertion; after removing it the same test passed 1/1.
 
 ## Focused verification
 
 - Current-source esbuild fixture red: previous desktop pin was 2.74 viewport heights and touch had no pin. After implementation, `npx playwright test tests/e2e/arrival-directors-cut.spec.ts --project=desktop-chromium --workers=1 --output=/tmp/directors-chromium-final2` passed 4/4: desktop and touch contexts progress/reverse, image bounds, reduced-motion cleanup, orientation refresh and overflow.
 - `PLAYWRIGHT_SKIP_VALIDATE_HOST_REQUIREMENTS=1 LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/tmp/zk17-libs/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu npx playwright test tests/e2e/arrival-directors-cut.spec.ts --project=iphone-webkit --workers=1 --output=/tmp/directors-webkit-final3` passed 4/4. Host-preflight bypass was necessary for the existing local GLES library; the managed WebKit browser and assertions ran. These fixture interactions set scroll position programmatically in a touch-enabled WebKit context; they do not prove a physical swipe, iOS browser-toolbar behavior, or device performance.
 - Scoped ESLint and `npm run typecheck` passed. This worker did not rebuild the shared export or run the integrated suite; controller owns those checks.
 - Source-fixture screenshots: `/tmp/directors-final-captures/desktop-{lights,smoke,hero,action,title}.png` and corresponding `mobile-*`. Those predate the last mobile action bounds fix. The revised action was recaptured and inspected at `/tmp/directors-final-captures/mobile-action-faded.png`; face and ball remain visible and the image edge fades. The fixture lacks the application font imports, so it is not evidence for final typography. Some photo-edge and secondary-player visibility remains for independent visual review. The controller must capture the built application and inspect all beats, no-JS/reduced motion, film transition, real font, and responsive framing.
 
 Old hero-only tests were updated for the new darkness, touch pin and photo source; header tests remain. An independent review and controller integration remain necessary before claiming the full brief is complete.
+
+## Independent review repair — round 1
+
+- Orientation: the hero records its normalized scroll position while the visitor is in the sequence, captures it before orientation/width refreshes, and restores it against the refreshed pin. Restoration is canceled on user input or hash changes and is limited to the hero sequence. Width bookkeeping also updates when rotation occurs at the opening or a pending restore is canceled. Existing story focus handling was not changed.
+- Smoke planes are overscanned and edge-faded, and their distinct scroll-linked movements continue throughout silhouette, portrait and montage beats. A source-fixture test confirms overscan and changed transform between 50% and 62%.
+- Photo treatment follows the actual source-image frame with horizontal and vertical soft fades and local dark shading over the secondary subject. No person is synthesized or automatically cut out. Captures of the rebuilt application were inspected at `/tmp/directors-r1-final/{desktop,mobile}-{smoke,hero,action}.png`; #17 remains legible and the teammate is dimmer. The game action remains a carrying pose, with limited source detail and some residual background figures. The controller's independent review remains the final visual gate.
+- The four photo-free fixture failures were caused by the smoke texture matching a broad photo-request regex; the assertion now matches the protected photo paths. Four obsolete identity-coordinate assertions now check visible ordering and non-overlap, and the tablet pin test explicitly requests motion. The separate null-film fixture now marks `/media/*` external to esbuild; film source was not edited.
+
+Validation:
+
+- On the pre-fix built app, the new midpoint rotation regression failed with normalized progress 0 instead of .5; the new smoke regression failed because its transform did not change.
+- On the rebuilt app, `PLAYWRIGHT_SKIP_VALIDATE_HOST_REQUIREMENTS=1 LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/tmp/zk17-libs/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu npx playwright test tests/e2e/arrival-directors-cut.spec.ts --grep 'built touch story|built story can' --project=desktop-chromium --project=iphone-webkit --workers=1 --output=/tmp/directors-r1-built-settled` passed 4/4. Both tests wait for the new pin distance, then recheck normalized progress after 400ms. One covers rotation at the opening followed by a second rotation mid-story. These use touch-enabled emulation and programmatic scroll, not a physical swipe.
+- The three affected integration cases passed 12/12 across the four configured projects (`/tmp/directors-r1-integrated`). The null-film fallback passed 4/4 (`/tmp/directors-r1-film-fallback`). The source-fixture smoke and sequence checks passed in Chromium and WebKit; the final WebKit focused run passed 3/3 (`/tmp/directors-r1-webkit-final3`). An earlier WebKit desktop-context fixture run intermittently failed on an opacity assertion placed near a transition; the final run seeks closer to the middle of each hold. The exact source of that timing variability was not independently established.
+- Scoped ESLint and `npm run typecheck` passed. The parent performed the production build and retains responsibility for the complete suite and final review. Physical iOS address-bar and hardware behavior are still unverified.
